<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Usage">Usage</span></h3>
<p>In order for the languages bar to function correctly each translated page must be created as a subpage of the original English page and the name of the subpage must be the language code, for example, "fr" for French. 
</p><p>Creating a subpage is done by adding a forward slash and the name of the subpage to the name of the parent page.
</p>
<pre>Parent_page/subpage
</pre>
<p>The languages bar can then be added to both the original English page and each of the translated pages. On the original English page the <b>PageName</b> parameter can be omitted so the following format is used:
</p>
<pre>{{Languages}}
</pre>
<p>On the translated page (regardless of language) the <b>PageName</b> parameter must be used to identify the original English page so the following format is used:
</p>
<pre>{{Languages|name-of-the-English-page}}
</pre>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Example">Example</span></h3>
<p>The location for the Russian translation of this page is <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Dragon%20Age%20Toolset%20Wiki%20-%20Language%20policy%20-%20ru" title="Dragon Age Toolset Wiki:Language policy/ru">Project:Language_policy/ru</a>. To display the language bar to this page we use <code>{{Languages}}</code> and to display the language bar (correctly) on the Russian version of this page we would use <code>{{Languages|Project:Language_policy}}</code>.
</p><p>We do <i>not</i> use <code>{{Languages|Project:Language_policy/ru}}</code> as the links to the original English page and any other translated pages would not be generated.
</p>
